    "['family evpn signaling', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'address-family l2vpn evpn', 'parent_command': ['aaa authentication login [parameter1] group [parameter2] local'], 'root': 'aaa authentication login [parameter1] group [parameter2] local', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\naddress-family l2vpn evpn\\nneighbor 3.3.3.3 activate\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command `set protocols bgp group evpn family evpn signaling` enables BGP to carry EVPN (Ethernet VPN) NLRI (Network Layer Reachability Information) for signaling purposes.\\n- In Cisco, this is configured under BGP's L2VPN EVPN address family, which needs to be activated for the specific neighbor (3.3.3.3 in this case).\\n- The Cisco command activates EVPN capability for the BGP session with the specified neighbor.\", 'trans_template': 'address-family l2vpn evpn'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 3.3.3.3 activate', 'parent_command': ['aaa authentication login [parameter1] group [parameter2] local'], 'root': 'aaa authentication login [parameter1] group [parameter2] local', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\naddress-family l2vpn evpn\\nneighbor 3.3.3.3 activate\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command `set protocols bgp group evpn family evpn signaling` enables BGP to carry EVPN (Ethernet VPN) NLRI (Network Layer Reachability Information) for signaling purposes.\\n- In Cisco, this is configured under BGP's L2VPN EVPN address family, which needs to be activated for the specific neighbor (3.3.3.3 in this case).\\n- The Cisco command activates EVPN capability for the BGP session with the specified neighbor.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 3.3.3.3 activate'}]]": 1,
